{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1102290-kung-fu-and-other-fight-styles-in-rules-updated-god-machine","id":1102290,"title":"Kung Fu and other Fight Styles in Rules Updated (God Machine)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-10T09:56:22-07:00","id":1102290,"title":"Kung Fu and other Fight Styles in Rules Updated (God Machine)","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> I saw that the fight styles that causes extra attacks were removed in the rules update, like Kung Fu, Two Weapons, Langschwertz (from Armory).<br /> Do you know if this happens because were too unbalanced? How do you use this in your campaign? Because such styles, like Two Weapons, is so common in games but I didn't see any references in the new rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9723-winchester","name":"winchester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T10:37:59-07:00","id":1102295,"title":"","content":"Since combat is abstractly designed, so that each 'attack' is not each time you move a limb towards an opponent with intent to cause harm, there is no need to allow an ability to offer multiple attacks, as they could just be represented with an addition to the diceroll.<br /> <br /> For instance, using Willpower. I could use my Willpower and get +3 to an attack. This could be, in-world, represented by my character using all his might to slam down in one powerful attack. But it could also be represented by him using all his energy to make a series of fast attacks.<br /> <br /> The end result is the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T10:49:19-07:00","id":1102298,"title":"","content":"They have pretty much killed multiple attacks in second edition. The only remnant is a sort of &quot;cleave&quot; effect in one style that lets you down one opponent and immediately go after another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T11:19:42-07:00","id":1102307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1102290-kung-fu-and-other-fight-styles-in-rules-updated-god-machine?p=1102298#post1102298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have pretty much killed multiple attacks in second edition. The only remnant is a sort of &quot;cleave&quot; effect in one style that lets you down one opponent and immediately go after another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Relentless Assault still has one, but with a hefty drawback and conditional, and it's at 5 dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T12:16:47-07:00","id":1102327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>winchester</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1102290-kung-fu-and-other-fight-styles-in-rules-updated-god-machine#post1102290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello!<br /> Do you know if this happens because were too unbalanced?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's because they were too unbalanced. Especially in first edition, let's say you have an 8-dice pool, and you can spend Willpower for an extra attack. That's almost mechanically identical to a +8 dice bonus on the one attack, which is over twice as much as a normal Willpower-costed bonus would give you, and runs over the normal +5 maximum for a single die bonus.<br /> <br /> There are a few effects in 2e that do similar things. Some give you an extra attack with a steeper cost and with more limits on how you can use it, like the Relentless Assault maneuver Effive and Malus mention. Some give you an extra means to output damage aside from making a conventional attack, like the area control maneuver in the new version of Martial Arts. None are going to give you an extra attack as easily as 1e Fighting Merits did, and really, those Merits never should have in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T14:36:45-07:00","id":1102362,"title":"","content":"Hurt Locker has the merits you are looking for in 2e. Generally speaking, others have addressed the issues and changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T19:57:52-07:00","id":1102418,"title":"","content":"There are also a few abilities that allow you to attack multiple targets with one attack, but with one very conditional exception you can't attack the same person multiple times in a turn.<br /> <br /> ...Unless you can reliably gain an exceptional success as a grappler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T01:54:28-07:00","id":1102463,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the two things you get to pick from the list in that case have to be different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T05:16:32-07:00","id":1102482,"title":"","content":"Even if that's true there are multiple grappling merits that allow you to deal damage while performing another action. Close Quarters Combat allows you to deal lethal while breaking free, Standing Throw/Takedown allows you to deal bashing while dropping the enemy prone, Joint Lock deals damage while also establishing a restrain. It's entirely possible to build a grappler where something like half of the possible moves on your list deal damage in addition to their normal effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T09:31:30-07:00","id":1102533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1102290-kung-fu-and-other-fight-styles-in-rules-updated-god-machine?p=1102482#post1102482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if that's true there are multiple grappling merits that allow you to deal damage while performing another action. Close Quarters Combat allows you to deal lethal while breaking free, Standing Throw/Takedown allows you to deal bashing while dropping the enemy prone, Joint Lock deals damage while also establishing a restrain. It's entirely possible to build a grappler where something like half of the possible moves on your list deal damage in addition to their normal effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but you can make anything similarly powerful with the right Merits. CofD doesn't shy away from letting characters be awesome at the stuff they invest EXP in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T10:00:12-07:00","id":1102545,"title":"","content":"Yes. The lack of multiple attacks per round does not mean characters can't deal out a lot of damage and crippling effects. There's no reason why it should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T03:42:34-07:00","id":1102754,"title":"","content":"HelmsDerp was just providing an example where you can deal multiple damaging moves against the same person, which is incredibly rare in 2E; not saying grappling is OP compared to other types of fighting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T15:23:08-07:00","id":1103632,"title":"","content":"Sure, some styles were really out of mind, like multiples attacks using Kung Fu.<br /> <br /> Another question about Second Ed, that i'm Reading now: with bigger defense (with the sum with Atlethics) is common that an attack roll goes to 0 (for example: 3 dex plus 3 atlethics = 6 defende, against a for + weaponry 3 = 6 dices, considering that the weapons doesn't increase the roll, only Automatic damage). In the situation with 0 dices to attack, ia that possible choose a focused attack in the Hand, for example, that penalizes with -4?<br /> <br /> I didn't play with the new rules, but my impression ia that the Melee combat will take a long time to finish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9723-winchester","name":"winchester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T15:51:36-07:00","id":1103637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>winchester</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1102290-kung-fu-and-other-fight-styles-in-rules-updated-god-machine?p=1103632#post1103632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question about Second Ed, that i'm Reading now: with bigger defense (with the sum with Atlethics) is common that an attack roll goes to 0 (for example: 3 dex plus 3 atlethics = 6 defende, against a for + weaponry 3 = 6 dices, considering that the weapons doesn't increase the roll, only Automatic damage). In the situation with 0 dices to attack, ia that possible choose a focused attack in the Hand, for example, that penalizes with -4?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you can spend Willpower and make an All-Out-Attack to bring that 0 dice up to 5. That gives you a pretty good chance of landing a hit. If you have a weapon and your goal is something other than violence for its own sake, that'll cause the Beaten Down Tilt, which pretty much takes your opponent out of the fight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>winchester</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1102290-kung-fu-and-other-fight-styles-in-rules-updated-god-machine?p=1103632#post1103632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't play with the new rules, but my impression ia that the Melee combat will take a long time to finish.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of people get this impression because for some reason they are averse to spending Willpower in combat, making All-Out-Attacks, or making Called Shots, and aren't used to considering the impact of Tilts. In practice, fights in 2e are very fast and very violent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T15:52:43-07:00","id":1103638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>winchester</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1102290-kung-fu-and-other-fight-styles-in-rules-updated-god-machine?p=1103632#post1103632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, some styles were really out of mind, like multiples attacks using Kung Fu.<br /> <br /> Another question about Second Ed, that i'm Reading now: with bigger defense (with the sum with Atlethics) is common that an attack roll goes to 0 (for example: 3 dex plus 3 atlethics = 6 defende, against a for + weaponry 3 = 6 dices, considering that the weapons doesn't increase the roll, only Automatic damage). In the situation with 0 dices to attack, ia that possible choose a focused attack in the Hand, for example, that penalizes with -4?<br /> <br /> I didn't play with the new rules, but my impression ia that the Melee combat will take a long time to finish.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes you can target still because you can go with a chance die; but you can't go below -5.<br /> <br /> You are also encouraged spend Willpower often, and/or use All Out Attack, don't skimp when your life is on the line. See also: Beaten Down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T07:04:32-07:00","id":1103793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1102290-kung-fu-and-other-fight-styles-in-rules-updated-god-machine?p=1103637#post1103637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you can spend Willpower and make an All-Out-Attack to bring that 0 dice up to 5. That gives you a pretty good chance of landing a hit. If you have a weapon and your goal is something other than violence for its own sake, that'll cause the Beaten Down Tilt, which pretty much takes your opponent out of the fight.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Make that attack a grapple and subsequent rolls don't have to contend with their defense but their contested brawl roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T08:24:41-07:00","id":1103817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1102290-kung-fu-and-other-fight-styles-in-rules-updated-god-machine?p=1103638#post1103638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes you can target still because you can go with a chance die; but you can't go below -5.<br /> <br /> You are also encouraged spend Willpower often, and/or use All Out Attack, don't skimp when your life is on the line. See also: Beaten Down.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Until -5 I can attack with a chance die and above that i cannot without the use of some maneveur or Willpower to increase this number, is that?<br /> Because if the character already have his dice roll 0, if he simple wishes to attack without any manner to increase this number, is rather focus on the weak spot, for example. One chance die for one chance die, it's better choose where hurts more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9723-winchester","name":"winchester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T08:57:10-07:00","id":1103822,"title":"","content":"I think the limit at -5 is a common house rule and not an official rule. As far as I remember only spellcasting in Mage is impossible to do below -5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T09:02:32-07:00","id":1103824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1102290-kung-fu-and-other-fight-styles-in-rules-updated-god-machine?p=1103822#post1103822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the limit at -5 is a common house rule and not an official rule. As far as I remember only spellcasting in Mage is impossible to do below -5.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I was just trying to explain that better and realized that I wasn't entirely sure where I got it from exactly. Generally, a given penalty shouldn't be more than a -5 and the Storyteller can decide when a task is impossible, but I don't think that -5 is a hard cutoff like I implied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T10:29:37-07:00","id":1103852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>winchester</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1102290-kung-fu-and-other-fight-styles-in-rules-updated-god-machine?p=1103817#post1103817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Until -5 I can attack with a chance die and above that i cannot without the use of some maneveur or Willpower to increase this number, is that?<br /> Because if the character already have his dice roll 0, if he simple wishes to attack without any manner to increase this number, is rather focus on the weak spot, for example. One chance die for one chance die, it's better choose where hurts more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two things, just to clarify and not saying you said otherwise. One, Willpower is not added to the end, it's part of the adding up of bonuses, which goes before the adding up of penalties.<br /> <br /> Two, regarding specified shots, most of them require a certain amount of damage to be done to do anything. Leg and Arm at a -2 require you to do the target's Stamina in damage, Head at -3 their Size, Heart a static 5. If you're rolling a Chance die you may not hit that damage threshold without some spectacular weapon. The exceptions are Eyes and Hands, the hardest parts to hit at a -4 and -5 respectively, which only require damage to be done to inflict a Tilt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-15-2017, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T10:43:19-07:00","id":1103858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1102290-kung-fu-and-other-fight-styles-in-rules-updated-god-machine?p=1103852#post1103852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Two things, just to clarify and not saying you said otherwise. One, Willpower is not added to the end, it's part of the adding up of bonuses, which goes before the adding up of penalties.<br /> <br /> Two, regarding specified shots, most of them require a certain amount of damage to be done to do anything. Leg and Arm at a -2 require you to do the target's Stamina in damage, Head at -3 their Size, Heart a static 5. If you're rolling a Chance die you may not hit that damage threshold without some spectacular weapon. The exceptions are Eyes and Hands, the hardest parts to hit at a -4 and -5 respectively, which only require damage to be done to inflict a Tilt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Called shots can also be useful for getting around armor (assuming there are exposed parts to target), even without extra effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}